#{[17592186426755 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426755 #edb/ref 1069 "q-10006" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426755 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426755 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & b \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ a & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426755 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06d7e42a-14b7-5ba4-9656-a3c1d06d273b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426755 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1069 "q-317636" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2z+3x-5=4 \\\\ 6z-4y+3=15 \\\\ 7y+2x-2=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-4$ | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $12$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $13$ |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5bfaecd0-980e-55a7-befc-289a7a9c5c34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426756 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+0y+2z=9 \\\\ 0x-4y+6z=12 \\\\ 2x+7y+0z=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1069 "q-317519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}8y+6x-3z+4=0 \\\\ 5z-3y+x-6=0 \\\\ 7x-4z-y-9=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $8$ | $-3$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $-4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $-1$ | $-4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $9$ |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87b42522-bb27-5dd3-ac3e-bd3279e82fdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426757 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+8y-3z=-4 \\\\ x-3y+5z=6 \\\\ 7x-y-4z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426758 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426758 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36179" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426758 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426758 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5z=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & a & 5 \\\\ b & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426758 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da13acd8-77ae-5f2b-ba9c-504353353d52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426758 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+5z=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=-1,\\,c=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
